  "text": "Seedbox tools",
  "note": "band title of the tools part (upper case on screen)."
 },
 "tp.about.a_seedbox_or_a": {
  "text": "A seedbox, or a media server that seeds, only does its job if it seeds as many of its media files as possible. Content that nothing seeds is wasted: the ratio does not grow and the trackers may even drop you. The three tools work with Prowlarr, Radarr, Sonarr and qBittorrent.",
  "note": "text of the folded \"What do the tools do?\" part."
 },
 "tp.about.find_my_torrent_looks": {
  "text": "<b>Find my torrent</b> looks for torrents (through Prowlarr) for the files in your downloads folders that nothing is seeding. <b>Shape up</b> (formerly Update me) searches every big, old, seeded title in the background and offers a smaller release, a better HDR format or a higher resolution, replaced through Radarr or Sonarr after you approve. <b>Season repacker</b> replaces the single episodes of a finished season with the season pack, so that one torrent seeds the whole season (the torrents it adds get the <code>seasonrepacker</code> tag); it can also watch autobrr for new season packs.",
  "note": "text of the folded \"What do the tools do?\" part. May contain simple HTML tags: keep them."
 },
 "tp.about.what_do_the_tools": {
  "text": "What do the tools do?",
  "note": "text of the folded \"What do the tools do?\" part."
 },
